There is a method of analysis used in remote sensing in
which a reference set of classification data are compared to
another data set (Congalton. 1999. Assessing the accuracy of
remotely sensed data.). In both data sets, items have been
placed into discrete classification  categories.  The
product is a square "error matrix" that gives the reference
classification in the columns and the other classfication in
the rows, where the columns and rows are the categories in
the classification.  The diagonal elements of the matrix are
the numbers of times the 2 data sets agree.  Nondiagonal
elements give the numbers of misclassified items by
category. 

My question is how I can produce such a table in S-Plus
(v.4.5) using predefined functions, or whether someone has
written functions for this kind of analysis?  The input data
table as I see it would consist of columns for the 2 data
sets for a large number of classified items in the rows of
the table. The data would of course be categorical (letter
codes for about 40 categories).

I am also looking for functions to analyze tables of this
kind statistically using the multinomial distribution.  

 
