From: Mike.Prager at noaa.gov (Michael Prager)
Date: Fri, 20 Aug 1999 15:00:07 -0400
Subject: [S] Summary: S-Plus Win 2000 crashes on exit
In-Reply-To: <37BCB03F.642163CB@trip.com.br>
References: <4.2.0.58.19990818115232.00a43840@mail.bea.nmfs.gov> <37BCB03F.642163CB@trip.com.br>
Message-ID: <4.2.0.58.19990820141401.00a37ee0@mail.bea.nmfs.gov>

Recently, I  wrote:

>> I am having a persistent problem with S-Plus 2000 Professional crashing on

exit [under Windows NT]. [...]  When I exit after using S-Plus for a while, 
it crashes and a "Dr. Watson" window comes up.  The bad part of this is 
that preferences [...] changed during the session are lost. <<

Responses:

Marcelo A. Ferreira Gomes reported that a colleague has had similar 
problems with several versions of S-Plus under Windows 95.

Stephen J. Smith reported that he is using S-Plus 2000 without problems.

Two replies from MathSoft stated that the problem was "that one of the 
files in your _Prefs directory is corrupt" and that I should either delete 
that directory or backup and delete the files there, one by one, to locate 
the faulty file.

In summary, the problem hasn't been resolved yet.  I trust that MathSoft 
can locate the cause of the corruption and if it's in S-Plus (the only 
program that accesses the _Prefs directory), fix it.

If anyone else experiences such crashes, please contact MathSoft to alert 
them to it.  With any luck, that will speed a cure.

My thanks to all who responded.

--
Michael Prager                     <Mike.Prager at noaa.gov>
NOAA Beaufort Laboratory
Beaufort, North Carolina  28516
