was trying to do was control the physical dimension on the plot according to
the value of the variables; that is, so that moving one centimeter to the
right means a change of 1 in the variable on the x-axis and moving one
centimeter up  means a change of 1 in the variable on the y-axis. The data
in question range from 0 to 10 on the x-axis and 0 to 5 on the y-axis. The
default S-PLUS plotting routines create a plot with the aspect ratio fairly
close to 1, but that is not what was asked for. What is desired I believe is
an aspect ratio of 1/2 (or 2, depending on how you define it).

