Subject: [S] HAC / Newey West
Message-ID: <852567DA.006134A9.00@pismtpmta01.putnaminv.com>

Hello:

I am running a regression that is both cross-sectional, time-series, and has
overlapping time periods.  I am wondering if anyone has created an lm() function
that adjusts for the overlap period by applying the Newey-West correction to the
residuals. This should increase the residuals and lower the t-stats.  It would
be a tremendous help if anyone has already created such a function, as it is a
fairly common problem in the field of finance.

Thanks,
