From V.Fidler at med.rug.nl  Mon Aug 30 11:28:58 1999
From: V.Fidler at med.rug.nl
Date: Mon, 30 Aug 1999 13:28:58 +0200
Subject: [S] Summary: importing data from SPSS
Message-ID: <199908301152.NAA10398@medmail.med.rug.nl>

A number of people kindly offered the - rather simple - solution. 
The import data dialog has an options menu which allows to choose 
for  'Import value labels as Numbers'. The corresponding function 
call is import.data()  with "VLabelAsNumber = F" as one of the 
arguments.

Many thanks to all who responded,
Vaclav Fidler

original question:

> I have a problem with importing data from an SPSS (.sav) file
> in Splus. Splus imports value labels rather than the values 
> themselves. Is there a way to change this unexpected
> behaviour? 
> Recoding in Splus or manually removing labels in SPSS is not 
really 
> an attractive option. There is a command syntax trick in SPSS for 
> suppressing labels (assinging a label to a single nonexistent value 
> only), but in this case Splus still imports labels only (=NA's).
> 
