On Mon, 30 Aug 1999, Julie Najita wrote:

> 
> Hi,
> 
> I'm running S-Plus 2000 on a PC and fitting a mixture model (described in
> Modern Applied Statistics with S-Plus, Venables & Ripley,1st ed, 4th
> printing).  I'd like to make the recommended changes to make.call() as
> indicated (p.242), however I can't seem to find this portion of the
> function.  I've made certain to attach the MASS library with first=T as the
> authors indicate.  Does anyone know whether make.call() underwent a change?

Yes, that change was incorporated in S-PLUS 2000, so is not in the S-PLUS
2000 version of the MASS library. The actual code we used was cleaned up
since the first edition.

> Has anyone tried out this example?

Yes, I have. No changes are needed to make.call in S-PLUS 2000.

Beware that you have the 1994 first edition of our book, and are using it
on a 1999 version of the program with the software from the 1999 third
edition, in the special version for S-PLUS 2000.  We tested all the 
examples from the third and second editions: we did not test those in the
first.  (To complicate matters, some of our changes were incorporated
in S-PLUS 2000 while out third edition was in press.)

